#15004
kallendbor lord man~
Lord Kallendbor~
Lord Kallendbor stands here waiting to hear from the latest king.~
He is an imposing figure. He stands almost seven feet tall and is
well muscled.  You would hate to have to fight him.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_TONGUES
0 S
30 0 BODY_HAND|BODY_FOOT 10d10+450 1d10+20
32892 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 2
  say You are welcome, $n, but I will not support a weak king.
else
  if quest(0, 4, $n) > 3
    if sex ($n) == 1
      say Welcome, High Lord $n
    else
      say Welcome, High Lady $n
    endif
  else
    nod $n
  endif
endif
~
>speech_prog fisticuffs~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 2
  say You challenge me at fisticuffs to determine if I
  say will bow to you?   I accept.  Defend yourself!
  mpkill $n
endif
~
>death_prog 100~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 2
  mpecho Kallendbor falls to the ground unconscious.
  mpecho Kallendbor regains consciousness and shakes his head as
  mpecho he gets to his feet.
  say You have defeated me in fair combat.
  say You will have my support.
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 4
  mpecho Kallendbor leaves to gather the support of his vassals.
  mppurge $i
endif
~
|
#15005
crow~
a Crow~
A Crow stands on a branch watching you.~
It has glossy black feathers crested in white.  It waits to see 
what you will do next.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_TONGUES
0 S
30 BODY_HEAD BODY_CLAW 10d10+450 1d10+20
10000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_FEMALE
>speech_prog Nightshade~
mpecho The crows eyes blink and suddenly turn blood-red.
mpecho The crow begins to change.  It seems to expand against the gloom,
mpecho shimmering with an aura of crimson light, its shadow rising up 
mpecho like a wraith set free.  The crimson aura dies away and the crow
mpecho is gone.  Nightshade now stands before you.
mpmload 15006
if quest(0, 4, $n) != 6
  mpforce nightshade mpkill $n
endif
mppurge $i
~
>rand_prog 100~
if quest(0, 4, $r) == 8
  mpecho The Crow shimmers as it turns into Nightshade.
  mpecho Nightshade tells you 'I will keep my promise, but you will pay
  mpecho for not slaying Strabo while you had the chance!'
  mpecho Nightshade turns back into a crow and flies away.
  mpmset $r quest 0 4 9
  mppurge $i
endif
~
|
#15006
nightshade witch~
Nightshade~
Nightshade stands here looking at you.~
She is tall and sharp-featured, her skin white and flawless, her hair 
raven black except for a single streak of white that runs down its center.
She is neither old nor young, but somewhere in between.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_TONGUES
-500 S
30 BODY_HEAD 0 10d10+450 1d10+20
10000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_FEMALE
>rand_prog 100~
if quest(0, 4, $r)== 6
  mpechoat $r Nightshade's face twists in anger and it looks as though you
  mpechoat $r have just become a corpse.
  shout You want me to bow down to you?
  mpechoat $r Nightshade's face suddenly relaxes and she smiles at you.
  say There is a way I would consider paying homage to you.
  say The dragon, Strabo, has been troubling me lately.
  say Take care of him and I will pledge my allegiance to you.
  mpoload 15004
  give dust $r
  say Use this dust on him, it will give you a slim
  say chance to succeed.
  cackle 
  mpmset $r quest 0 4 7
  mpecho Nightshade turns back into a crow and flies away.
  mppurge $i
else
  mpoload 15004
  mpkill $r
endif
~
|
#15007
river master~
The River master~
The River Master is here waiting to hear your speech.~
He is a lean figure with a slim silver diadem about his forehead.
His skin is of a silver cast, almost scaled, but his hair is black and
thick about the nape of his neck and forearms.  He has the look of 
something carved out of wood.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_TONGUES
0 S
40 BODY_HEAD BODY_HAND 10d10+600 1d10+30
10000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 5
  say I understand that you have conned Kallendbor into
  say following you He is a wimp.  I will not be so easy
  say to cozen.
else
  if quest(0, 4, $n) > 11
    if sex ($n) == 1
      say Good to see you again, Son.
    else
      say Good to see you again, Daughter.
    endif
  else
    nod $n
  endif
endif
~
>speech_prog daughter marriage.~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 5
  if sex ($n) == 1
    say You have discovered that they way to get to me is
    say through my daughter.  Very well, You may wed my
    say daughter if you can win the support of both
    say Nightshade and Strabo.
    mpecho The River Master smiles triumphantly.
    mpmset $n quest 0 4 6
  endif
endif
~
>speech_prog son marriage.~
if quest(0, 4, $n) == 5
  if sex ($n) != 1
    say You have discovered that they way to get to me
    say is through my son.  Very well, You may wed my son
    say if you can win the support of both Nightshade and
    say Strabo.
    mpecho The River Master smiles triumphantly.
    mpmset $n quest 0 4 6
  endif
endif
~
